<title>USA: U.S. HEADLINE STOCKS - Issues to watch - Aug 26.</title>
<headline>U.S. HEADLINE STOCKS - Issues to watch - Aug 26.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stocks to watch this morning:</p>
<p>* MFS Communications Co Inc and WorldCom Inc said they agreed on a $14 billion merger under which each MFS share will be swapped for 2.1 WorldCom shares. MFS closed at 34-7/8 on Friday, while WorldCom closed at 26-3/8.</p>
<p>* Columbus McKinnon Corp said it agreed to acquire Spreckels Industries Inc. Columbus said the pact calls for it to begin a $24 per share tender offer for Spreckels. Spreckels closed at 19-3/8, and Columbus McKinnon closed at 14-3/4.  </p>
<p>* Advanced Medical Inc said it agreed to acquire privately-held IVAC Medical Systems Inc in a $400 million cash deal. Advanced Medical closed at 2-7/16.</p>
<p>* British Airways Plc is close to placing an order for up to 30 Boeing Co aircraft worth nearly $4 billion, the London Times reported. British Airways American depositary shares closed at 82-1/2, Boeing closed at 90-3/8.  </p>
<p>-- Wall Street Desk 212-859-1730</p>
